<title>GERMANY: Hoechst shares plunge 13 percent.</title>
<headline>Hoechst shares plunge 13 percent.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hoechst AG plunged 10 percent in active bourse dealings after the German chemical and pharmaceuticals group said it would not list its Hoechst Marion Roussel (HMR) unit on the stock market.</p>
<p>At 1000 GMT, Hoechst shares were down 9.95 marks to a daily low at 68.60 marks. Dealers said the market was surprised and disappointed at the news that Hoechst no longer planned to list HMR, a move that had been widely expected.</p>
<p>&quot;The announcement today has taken all speculative interest out of the stock,&quot; said one London-based trader.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
